# Example OBJ with two named meshes: a regular icosahedron and a regular dodecahedron.
# Coordinates use phi = (1 + sqrt(5)) / 2 ~= 1.618034.
# The icosahedron is centered at (-2.5, 0, 0) and the dodecahedron at (2.5, 0, 0).
# Dodecahedron faces are written as pentagons (fan-triangulated on load).

o Icosahedron
v -2.500000  1.000000  1.618034
v -2.500000 -1.000000  1.618034
v -2.500000  1.000000 -1.618034
v -2.500000 -1.000000 -1.618034
v -1.500000  1.618034  0.000000
v -3.500000  1.618034  0.000000
v -1.500000 -1.618034  0.000000
v -3.500000 -1.618034  0.000000
v -0.881966  0.000000  1.000000
v -4.118034  0.000000  1.000000
v -0.881966  0.000000 -1.000000
v -4.118034  0.000000 -1.000000
f 1 2 9
f 1 9 5
f 1 5 6
f 1 6 10
f 1 10 2
f 2 10 8
f 2 8 7
f 2 7 9
f 9 7 11
f 9 11 5
f 5 11 3
f 5 3 6
f 6 3 12
f 6 12 10
f 10 12 8
f 8 12 4
f 8 4 7
f 7 4 11
f 4 12 3
f 4 3 11

